This reminds me of a patch I made ages ago, but never quite finished.
It added an intermediate 'dim' light level the the game. Monsters and
items in the dimly lit porition of the map showed up in monochrome, and
could not be fully identified with '?'. So a dwarf would appear as a
grey 'h' and would be identified as a "humanoid".

I made all normal light sources have a dim outer fringe, which meant
wandering in the dark with a lamp was a little riskier as you could not
fully identify monsters until they got close. I also made telepathy
only display monsters dimly, so you could sense that there were a group
of 'o's on the level, but no whether they were goblins or Uruk-hai.

It was a lot of work. I wonder where I left it.

